      "hints": [
        "Set $\\frac{x - 3}{x} = \\frac{x - 5}{x - 3} \\implies (x - 3)^2 = x(x - 5)$ and solve for $x = 9$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Equate the common ratios for the three consecutive terms $x, x - 3, x - 5$:\n$$\\frac{x - 3}{x} = \\frac{x - 5}{x - 3}$$",
        "Cross-multiply and expand:\n$$(x - 3)^2 = x(x - 5) \\implies x^2 - 6x + 9 = x^2 - 5x$$\n$$-6x + 9 = -5x \\implies x = 9$$"
      ],
